[recv] {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"commandExecution","id":"call_6eGDtkHVCtMyEnrfpsogt6FM","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/trace.md\"","cwd":"/workspace","processId":"64344","source":"unifiedExecStartup","status":"completed","commandActions":[{"type":"read","command":"sed -n '1,200p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/trace.md","name":"trace.md","path":"/root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/trace.md"}],"aggregatedOutput":"# `<trace />`\n\nThe `<trace />` element represents an electrical connection between two or more points in your circuit. Traces can connect components, nets, or specific pins on components.\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nexport default () => (\n  <board width=\"10mm\" height=\"10mm\">\n    <resistor name=\"R1\" resistance=\"1k\" footprint=\"0402\" pcbX={-2} schX={-2} />\n    <capacitor name=\"C1\" capacitance=\"100nF\" footprint=\"0402\" pcbX={2} />\n    <trace\n      from=\".R1 > .pin1\"\n      to=\".C1 > .pin1\"\n    />\n  </board>\n)\n```\n\n## Props\n\nCommonly used: `via`, `fromLayer`, `toLayer`, `code`, `message`, `path`, `key`, `thickness`\n\n## References\n\n- Props: [TraceProps](https://github.com/tscircuit/props#traceprops-trace)\n- Source: [lib/components/trace.ts](https://github.com/tscircuit/props/blob/main/lib/components/trace.ts)\n- Local docs: [docs/docs/elements/trace.mdx](../docs/docs/elements/trace.mdx)\n","exitCode":0,"durationMs":0},"threadId":"019e8ebe-3350-7570-90f8-ccea92f86cdd","turnId":"019e8ebe-335b-7063-9c14-de69357ce45c","completedAtMs":1780511378817}}
